   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Forms of zijn and inversion",
     "texto": [
      "In the present tense, the irregular verb «zijn» (to be) has these forms: «ik ben» (I am), «jij bent» (you are), «u bent» (you are, formal), «hij/zij/het is» (he/she/it is) and «wij/jullie/zij zijn» (we/you all/they are). Key rule: in questions, or after inversion with the second-person pronoun «jij/je» placed after the verb, the verb always loses its final -t: «Ben je ziek?» (Are you ill?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
